index 4479b53..5ac51d1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,27 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The shared layout registers browser-mediated tools with `document.modelContext`
+(and detects the legacy `navigator.modelContext` entry point). Browsers without
+WebMCP continue to work normally; no global polyfill or external MCP server is installed.
+Registration follows the [WebMCP draft](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/)
+and lasts across Astro client navigation. Registrations use an AbortSignal for hot reload cleanup.
+
+| Tool | Arguments | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `query`, optional `limit` (1–50, default 10) | Search titles and summaries, return article metadata and URLs. |
+| `get_reading_list` | none | Return saved articles for the current session. |
+| `set_article_saved` | `slug`, `saved` (boolean) | Explicitly save or remove an article, updating visible bookmarks and an open reading list. |
+| `open_article` | `slug` | Open a known article in this tab using Astro navigation. |
+
+Use a WebMCP-capable browser agent to discover and invoke these tools. Slugs come
+from search results. Invalid arguments, unknown articles, and failed requests reject
+with descriptive errors. Fetches accept execution cancellation signals. Tools use
+the same first-party session and client actions as the UI. The reading-list endpoint
+still accepts the original `{ slug }` toggle request, and also accepts `{ slug, saved }`
+for repeatable explicit updates. Article summaries returned by tools are untrusted content.
+
+Run `npm test` for automated tool contract checks and `npm run build` for the production build.
